<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
           elementFormDefault="qualified">

  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
      Purpose
      -------
      RESPONSE envelope returned by the customer search operation findCustomersB
      (verified against the loyalty-app service generation, 2026-10).

      Namespace
      ---------
      The service emits the response without any namespace declaration (plain
      &lt;RESPONSE ResponseId="..."&gt;), so this schema has no target namespace. Earlier revisions
      declared one, which no real response could satisfy.

      Shapes
      ------
      Success (one or more customers found):
        RESPONSE @ResponseId, RESPONSE_DATE, then one CUSTOMER block per customer (1 to 50).
        A success response carries NO RESPONSE_CODE and no count / paging elements.
      Not found:
        RESPONSE @ResponseId, RESPONSE_DATE, RESPONSE_CODE (E163 in the loyalty-app service
        generation; E105 in the older service generation), optionally RESPONSE_DATA holding
        phone-validation details as child elements.
      Request / validation error:
        RESPONSE @ResponseId, RESPONSE_DATE, RESPONSE_CODE.
      Internal error with diagnostics enabled (E1006):
        RESPONSE @ResponseId, RESPONSE_DATE, [CUSTOMER blocks built so far], a second
        RESPONSE_DATE, RESPONSE_CODE, RESPONSE_DATA holding the exception text.
      Unhandled failure (E999):
        RESPONSE (no ResponseId), an EMPTY RESPONSE_DATE, RESPONSE_CODE.

      Because RESPONSE_DATE can repeat and the blocks can interleave, the content model is an
      unordered, repeat-tolerant choice. Consumers should read RESPONSE_CODE first: absent means
      success.

      Timestamps are "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S" strings (1 to 3 fractional digits, server local
      time), not ISO 8601.
    </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>

  <xs:complexType name="ResponseDataType" mixed="true">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>
        RESPONSE_DATA has two forms:
          (a) with E1006: plain text - the internal exception message;
          (b) with the "not found" code, when phone validation is enabled for the deployment and
              the validation service returned details: a set of child elements, one per detail
              returned, each named by the UPPER-CASED key supplied by the validation provider and
              holding a text value. The element names are provider-defined and not fixed by the
              service, hence the open content.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:any namespace="##any" processContents="lax" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded"/>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="MktSegmentsType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Container, always emitted inside the contact section (may be empty).</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="MKT_SEGMENT" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Marketing segment code assigned to the customer, most recently assigned first. The number returned is limited by deployment configuration (default 2).</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="CrossReferenceType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>One external-system identifier held by the customer.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:sequence>
      <xs:element name="SYSTEM_REFERENCE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Identifier type (e.g. POS_ID, LOYALTY_ID). Same value domain as SYSTEM_REFERENCE in the request.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="SYSTEM_REFERENCE_ID" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Identifier value.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:sequence>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:complexType name="CustomerType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>
        One matched customer. Emission order in the loyalty-app service generation:
          identity   FIRST_NAME, LAST_NAME, BIRTHDAY, GENDER, CUSTOMER_ID, REQ_REWARD_POINTS,
                     EV_BALANCE, CASHIER, ASSIGNED_STORE                       (always present)
          address    ADDRESS1, ADDRESS2, CITY, [STATE], ZIP, COUNTRY,
                     BAD_POSTAL_ADDRESS_STATUS, ALLOW_SOLICITATION             (1st ALLOW_SOLICITATION)
          e-mail     EMAIL_ID, BAD_EMAIL_ADDRESS_STATUS, ALLOW_SOLICITATION    (2nd ALLOW_SOLICITATION)
          phone      [PHONE_NUMBER, ALLOW_SOLICITATION]                        (3rd ALLOW_SOLICITATION)
          segments   MKT_SEGMENTS
          references CROSS_REFERENCE (0..n)
          POS        POS_SEGMENT
        ALLOW_SOLICITATION therefore appears up to THREE times with different meanings; its meaning
        is given by its position (it follows the block it belongs to). STATE is only emitted when a
        postal address exists. The phone pair is omitted entirely when the customer has a primary
        phone but its solicitation setting suppresses display. The address / e-mail / phone /
        segments section can be cut short if an internal data error occurs while it is built, so
        every element is optional and the model is an unordered, repeat-tolerant choice.
        Elements carrying no data are emitted EMPTY rather than omitted.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
      <xs:element name="FIRST_NAME" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>First name. The literal "Guest" is returned for a customer who is not enrolled in the loyalty programme (the real name is withheld). Empty when not recorded.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="LAST_NAME" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Last name. The literal "Customer" is returned for a customer who is not enrolled in the loyalty programme. Empty when not recorded.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="BIRTHDAY" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Date of birth as "yyyy-MM-dd", or empty when not recorded.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="GENDER" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>One of MALE, FEMALE, UNKNOWN, or empty when no gender is recorded.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="CUSTOMER_ID" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Customer identifier (the value to use as CUSTOMER_ID in other operations).</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="REQ_REWARD_POINTS" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Whole number (integer text, "0" when none): points the customer still needs to reach the next reward.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="EV_BALANCE" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Loyalty points balance (earned minus redeemed) as decimal text; "0" when the customer has no loyalty identifier or no points. Not rounded: a fractional balance can carry many decimal digits.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="CASHIER" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Cashier / associate reference stored on the customer record; usually empty.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="ASSIGNED_STORE" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Home store assigned to the customer, or empty.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="ADDRESS1" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Primary postal address, line 1. Empty when the customer has no current primary postal address.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="ADDRESS2" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Primary postal address, line 2, or empty.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="CITY" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>City, or empty.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="STATE" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>State / province code. Emitted only when a primary postal address exists (ABSENT, not empty, otherwise).</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="ZIP" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>ZIP / postal code, upper-cased, or empty.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="COUNTRY" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Country code, or empty.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="BAD_POSTAL_ADDRESS_STATUS" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Y or N. N only when the customer's address has been verified and is not flagged invalid; Y in every other case, including "no address on file".</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="ALLOW_SOLICITATION" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Solicitation (contact permission) flag for the block it follows: 1st occurrence = postal address, 2nd = e-mail, 3rd = phone. Values: Y (allowed), N (not allowed), U (unknown), or empty when the block has no data or no flag is stored.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="EMAIL_ID" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Primary e-mail address. Empty when the customer has none, or when the solicitation setting for the address suppresses display.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="BAD_EMAIL_ADDRESS_STATUS" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Y or N. N when an e-mail address is returned and is not flagged invalid; Y when it is flagged invalid or when EMAIL_ID is empty.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="PHONE_NUMBER" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Primary phone as area code + number, digits concatenated, no country code. Empty when the customer has no primary phone; ABSENT (together with the 3rd ALLOW_SOLICITATION) when a phone exists but its solicitation setting suppresses display.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="MKT_SEGMENTS" type="MktSegmentsType">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Marketing segments container (may be empty).</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="CROSS_REFERENCE" type="CrossReferenceType">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Repeats once per external-system identifier held by the customer (zero or more). A LOYALTY_ID reference is withheld for a customer who is not enrolled in the loyalty programme.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
      <xs:element name="POS_SEGMENT" type="xs:string">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation>Point-of-sale segment code for the customer, or empty.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:element>
    </xs:choice>
  </xs:complexType>

  <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>
        Top-level response container. See the schema header for the shapes.
      </xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:choice minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Server timestamp, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.S" (e.g. 2026-10-12 15:03:00.655). Always the first child. Emitted a second time on E1006; EMPTY on E999.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string">
          <xs:annotation>
            <xs:documentation>
              Outcome code. ABSENT on success. Open string - the catalog below is documentation,
              not a restriction, so new codes cannot break validation.
                E101  XmlInput parameter missing or empty
                E102  request XML not well-formed
                E103  XML parser configuration error
                E104  I/O error reading the request XML
                E105  no usable search filter supplied (see the request schema for which filters
                      count). In the older service generation E105 is ALSO returned when no
                      customer matches.
                E127  STORE_ID supplied but unknown (or no store is configured)
                E163  no customer matched the search (loyalty-app service generation). Routine
                      traffic: it normally precedes new-customer enrollment. May be accompanied by
                      RESPONSE_DATA.
                E899  access token missing or invalid (rejected before the search runs)
                E999  unhandled failure
                E1006 internal error; emitted only when diagnostics are enabled for the
                      deployment, with the exception text in RESPONSE_DATA
              Consumers should treat E105 and E163 alike as "not found" unless they sent no filters.
            </xs:documentation>
          </xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATA" type="ResponseDataType">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Error detail text (E1006) or phone-validation details (not found). See ResponseDataType.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
        <xs:element name="CUSTOMER" type="CustomerType">
          <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>One block per matched customer; 1 to 50 on success, in no guaranteed order. Absent on "not found" and on errors.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:choice>
      <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string" use="optional">
        <xs:annotation><xs:documentation>Server-assigned log / correlation identifier for this call. Present on every response except E999.</xs:documentation></xs:annotation>
      </xs:attribute>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>


  <xs:element name="WEBSERVICE">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>Gate-error envelope of the older service generation: when the tenant key (E888) or the access token (E899) is rejected before the operation runs, the response is WEBSERVICE / RESPONSE / RESPONSE_CODE only - no RESPONSE_DATE and no ResponseId. The loyalty-app service generation returns the same errors as a bare RESPONSE root with RESPONSE_DATE and RESPONSE_CODE.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:complexType>
      <xs:sequence>
        <xs:element name="RESPONSE">
          <xs:complexType>
            <xs:sequence>
              <xs:element name="RESPONSE_DATE" type="xs:string" minOccurs="0"/>
              <xs:element name="RESPONSE_CODE" type="xs:string"/>
            </xs:sequence>
            <xs:attribute name="ResponseId" type="xs:string"/>
          </xs:complexType>
        </xs:element>
      </xs:sequence>
    </xs:complexType>
  </xs:element>
</xs:schema>
